---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const reconstructInstructionResult = await reconstructInstruction(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const compareScopeResult = await compareScope(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, reconstructInstructionResult.accepted);
const traceDependenciesResult = await traceDependencies(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, compareScopeResult.accepted);
const formOptionsResult = await formOptions(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, traceDependenciesResult.accepted);
const assembleChangeResult = await assembleChange(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, formOptionsResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { reconstructInstruction: reconstructInstructionResult, compareScope: compareScopeResult, traceDependencies: traceDependenciesResult, formOptions: formOptionsResult, assembleChange: assembleChangeResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...reconstructInstructionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...compareScopeResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...traceDependenciesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...formOptionsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...assembleChangeResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...reconstructInstructionResult.checks, ...compareScopeResult.checks, ...traceDependenciesResult.checks, ...formOptionsResult.checks, ...assembleChangeResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A verbal instruction is later disputed: preserve contemporaneous evidence and request formal confirmation. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve contemporaneous evidence and request formal confirmation.) through the existing stage result for SiteInstruction; preserve exact source/version and the prior SiteInstruction, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A drawing revision changes only one area: avoid applying it to the whole project. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (avoid applying it to the whole project.) through the existing stage result for SiteInstruction; preserve exact source/version and the prior SiteInstruction, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Work began before commercial approval: record actual events without backdating authority. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (record actual events without backdating authority.) through the existing stage result for SiteInstruction; preserve exact source/version and the prior SiteInstruction, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A delay claim ignores available float: use exact schedule analysis and explicit assumptions. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (use exact schedule analysis and explicit assumptions.) through the existing stage result for SiteInstruction; preserve exact source/version and the prior SiteInstruction, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — Two changes affect the same work: prevent duplicate cost attribution. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (prevent duplicate cost attribution.) through the existing stage result for SiteInstruction; preserve exact source/version and the prior SiteInstruction, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, reconstructInstruction: reconstructInstructionResult, compareScope: compareScopeResult, traceDependencies: traceDependenciesResult, formOptions: formOptionsResult, assembleChange: assembleChangeResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
